<title>PAKISTAN: Mobil joint-venture to sell lubricants in Pakistan.</title>
<headline>Mobil joint-venture to sell lubricants in Pakistan.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-07-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mobil Corp, said on Saturday it will launch a wide range of lubricants in Pakistan in the next few weeks and capture at least 10 percent of market share in one year.</p>
<p>The firm would get at least 10 percent share in the market, where annual sales touch 250,000 tonnes, said Mark Green, President of Mobil Askari Lubricants Ltd, who has set up the joint venture with the Army Welfare Trust in Pakistan.</p>
<p>Green said Mobil's present $10 million investment in the joint ventures in Pakistan could rise. Mobil purchased a blending plant in Pakistan last year and production would start next month, he said.</p>
<p>-- Karachi Newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
